<title>UK: Sheffield Utd to join stock market says Times.</title>
<headline>Sheffield Utd to join stock market says Times.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British football club Sheffield United is set to become a listed company when it reveals a reverse takeover of leisurewear company Conrad Plc on Wednesday, the Times reported.</p>
<p>Sheffield United is currently in second place in England's First Division, which is the level below the Premier League.</p>
<p>The Times said Conrad will pay 9.5 million stg for the football club and the group will launch a 12 million stg rights offering.</p>
<p>The club is aiming for promotion to the Premier League and the Times said it was offering some players share incentives.</p>
<p>Conrad said in October it was in talks with Sheffield Utd.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
